From: Nicolas Michaut <nicolas@yumilab.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sunxi: boot from USB first when a system is plugged in
Date: 2026-10-11

The H3 boot ROM only starts from the SD card, so U-Boot always comes from
it, but the operating system it then loads can live elsewhere. Try USB
storage before the SD card: a USB stick holding a system boots instead
of the one on the card, which is left untouched. That gives a rescue
path when the card's system no longer boots while U-Boot, in a raw area
nothing writes to, still does, and a way to try another system without
reflashing the card. With no USB storage plugged in, the SD card boots
as before.

Signed-off-by: Nicolas Michaut <nicolas@yumilab.com>
---
--- a/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
+++ b/include/configs/sunxi-common.h
@@ -220,9 +220,9 @@
 
 #define BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES(func) \
 	func(FEL, fel, na) \
+	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_USB(func) \
 	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_MMC(func) \
 	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_SCSI(func) \
-	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_USB(func) \
 	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_PXE(func) \
 	BOOT_TARGET_DEVICES_DHCP(func)
 
